.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-START-QUEUE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-start-queue \- let a stopped queue be received from again
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eqs start-queue
.BR \-\-queue | \-q
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clears what
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-stop-queue (1)
recorded, so
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-receive-messages (1)
is answered normally again.
.PP
Consumers that have been polling and failing pick up on their next
attempt \- nothing has to be restarted \- and whatever accumulated while
the queue was stopped is delivered in the ordinary way, oldest first
within each priority.
.PP
Starting a queue that was never stopped changes nothing and is not an
error, so this is safe to run without checking first.
.PP
Be aware of what has built up: a queue stopped for an hour under load
has an hour of messages in it, and every consumer resumes at once
against that backlog. Check with
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-count (1)
before starting if the answer might matter.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-queue " " \fIERN\fR
ERN of the queue to start. Required. Resolve a name to its ERN with
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-ern (1).
.SH OUTPUT
The JSON response is printed to standard output:
.RS
.TP
.I ern
The queue that was started.
.TP
.I status
.I AVAILABLE
\- what is now recorded for it.
.TP
.I available
How many messages are receivable at this moment, i.e. the backlog
consumers are about to be handed.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The queue is recorded as running again.
.TP
.B 1
The queue ERN is missing or names no queue, the caller is not authorized
for it, the request could not be sent, or the server rejected it.
Details are printed to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the backlog, then let consumers back in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs get-message-count \e
    --queue ern:eqs:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:queue:onix-queue

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs start-queue \e
    --queue ern:eqs:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:queue:onix-queue
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-stop-queue (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-receive-messages (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-count (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
